              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "0.35n+5=0.48(n+5)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the original number of students and $b$ the original number with blue eyes. Then $b=0.35n$. After five blue-eyed students join,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{b+5}{n+5}&=0.48\\\\b+5&=0.48(n+5)\\\\0.35n+5&=0.48(n+5)\\\\35n+500&=48(n+5)\\\\35n+500&=48n+240\\\\260&=13n\\\\n&=\\frac{260}{13}\\\\n&=20\\end{align*}$$\nThere were originally 20 students.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
